<title>JAPAN: Petrolub International to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Petrolub International to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petrolub International Co Ltd said on Monday that it plans to buy back up to 70,000 of its shares at a cost not exceeding 70 million yen.</p>
<p>Shares of Petrolub, a distributor of auto lubricants, stood at 1,050 yen at 0700 GMT, down from the previous close of 1,080 yen.</p>
<p>The company's major shareholder is British Petroleum Co Plc.</p>
</text>
